[{"input":"# Lecture 4 – Computer Hardware and Architecture\n\n## Learning Objectives\n\nAt the end of this chapter, students should be able to:\n\n- Identify the major hardware components of a computer.\n- Explain the roles of the CPU, memory, storage, and input/output devices.\n- Understand the Von Neumann architecture.\n- Explain how a processor executes instructions.\n- Understand the roles of registers, cache memory, RAM, and storage.\n- Explain why memory hierarchy exists.\n- Understand how hardware components communicate.\n- Recognize the role of GPUs and specialized processors.","output":"","result":"Lecture 4 – Computer Hardware and Architecture\nLearning Objectives\nAt the end of this chapter, students should be able to:\n\nIdentify the major hardware components of a computer.\n\nExplain the roles of the CPU, memory, storage, and input/output devices.\n\nUnderstand the Von Neumann architecture.\n\nExplain how a processor executes instructions.\n\nUnderstand the roles of registers, cache memory, RAM, and storage.\n\nExplain why memory hierarchy exists.\n\nUnderstand how hardware components communicate.\n\nRecognize the role of GPUs and specialized processors.\n\n","resultHTML":"<h1 id=\"md-13g62dh-1993-1objkgm-lecture-4-computer-hardware-and-architecture\">Lecture 4 – Computer Hardware and Architecture</h1>\n<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-1993-1objkgm-learning-objectives\">Learning Objectives</h2>\n<p>At the end of this chapter, students should be able to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Identify the major hardware components of a computer.\n</li>\n<li>Explain the roles of the CPU, memory, storage, and input/output devices.\n</li>\n<li>Understand the Von Neumann architecture.\n</li>\n<li>Explain how a processor executes instructions.\n</li>\n<li>Understand the roles of registers, cache memory, RAM, and storage.\n</li>\n<li>Explain why memory hierarchy exists.\n</li>\n<li>Understand how hardware components communicate.\n</li>\n<li>Recognize the role of GPUs and specialized processors.\n</li>\n</ul>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown"},{"input":"## Introduction\n\nIn the previous chapter, we learned how electronic circuits can:\n\n- Represent data\n- Perform calculations\n- Store information\n\nUsing:\n\n- Logic gates\n- Adders\n- Flip-flops\n- Registers\n\nWe can now answer a larger question:  \nHow are these building blocks assembled into a complete computer?\n\nModern computers are composed of several subsystems working together:\n\n```text\n+------------------+\n|      CPU         |\n+------------------+\n         |\n         |\n+------------------+\n|      Memory      |\n+------------------+\n         |\n         |\n+------------------+\n|     Storage      |\n+------------------+\n         |\n         |\n+------------------+\n| Input / Output   |\n+------------------+\n```\n\n","output":"","result":"Introduction\nIn the previous chapter, we learned how electronic circuits can:\n\nRepresent data\n\nPerform calculations\n\nStore information\n\n\nUsing:\n\nLogic gates\n\nAdders\n\nFlip-flops\n\nRegisters\n\n\nWe can now answer a larger question:  \nHow are these building blocks assembled into a complete computer?\nModern computers are composed of several subsystems working together:\n+------------------+\n|      CPU         |\n+------------------+\n         |\n         |\n+------------------+\n|      Memory      |\n+------------------+\n         |\n         |\n+------------------+\n|     Storage      |\n+------------------+\n         |\n         |\n+------------------+\n| Input / Output   |\n+------------------+","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-1994-cz4ht7-introduction\">Introduction</h2>\n<p>In the previous chapter, we learned how electronic circuits can:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Represent data\n</li>\n<li>Perform calculations\n</li>\n<li>Store information\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Using:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Logic gates\n</li>\n<li>Adders\n</li>\n<li>Flip-flops\n</li>\n<li>Registers\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>We can now answer a larger question:  \nHow are these building blocks assembled into a complete computer?</p>\n<p>Modern computers are composed of several subsystems working together:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>+------------------+\n|      CPU         |\n+------------------+\n         |\n         |\n+------------------+\n|      Memory      |\n+------------------+\n         |\n         |\n+------------------+\n|     Storage      |\n+------------------+\n         |\n         |\n+------------------+\n| Input / Output   |\n+------------------+</code></pre>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown"},{"input":"## The Von Neumann Architecture\n\nMost modern computers follow a design proposed by mathematician John von Neumann.  \nThis design remains the basis of nearly all computers today.\n\n### Main Components\n\nThe architecture consists of:\n\n#### Processor (CPU)\n\nExecutes instructions.\n\n#### Main Memory (RAM)\n\nStores programs and data currently being used.\n\n#### Storage\n\nStores information permanently.\n\n#### Input and Output Devices\n\nAllow interaction with the outside world.\n\n### Conceptual Diagram\n\n```text\n                 +---------+\n                 |  Input  |\n                 +---------+\n                      |\n                      ↓\n+---------+ <--> +---------+ <--> +----------+\n| Storage |      | Memory  |      |   CPU    |\n+---------+ <--> +---------+ <--> +----------+\n                      |\n                      ↓\n                 +---------+\n                 | Output  |\n                 +---------+\n```\n\n### Fundamental Idea\n\nPrograms and data are stored in memory.  \nThe processor repeatedly:\n\n- Fetches an instruction.\n- Executes the instruction.\n- Moves to the next instruction.\n\nThis idea forms the basis of modern computing.","output":"","result":"The Von Neumann Architecture\nMost modern computers follow a design proposed by mathematician John von Neumann.  \nThis design remains the basis of nearly all computers today.\nMain Components\nThe architecture consists of:\nProcessor (CPU)\nExecutes instructions.\nMain Memory (RAM)\nStores programs and data currently being used.\nStorage\nStores information permanently.\nInput and Output Devices\nAllow interaction with the outside world.\nConceptual Diagram\n                 +---------+\n                 |  Input  |\n                 +---------+\n                      |\n                      ↓\n+---------+ <--> +---------+ <--> +----------+\n| Storage |      | Memory  |      |   CPU    |\n+---------+ <--> +---------+ <--> +----------+\n                      |\n                      ↓\n                 +---------+\n                 | Output  |\n                 +---------+\nFundamental Idea\nPrograms and data are stored in memory.  \nThe processor repeatedly:\n\nFetches an instruction.\n\nExecutes the instruction.\n\nMoves to the next instruction.\n\n\nThis idea forms the basis of modern computing.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-1995-h2qcc1-the-von-neumann-architecture\">The Von Neumann Architecture</h2>\n<p>Most modern computers follow a design proposed by mathematician John von Neumann.  \nThis design remains the basis of nearly all computers today.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-1995-h2qcc1-main-components\">Main Components</h3>\n<p>The architecture consists of:</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-1995-h2qcc1-processor-cpu\">Processor (CPU)</h4>\n<p>Executes instructions.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-1995-h2qcc1-main-memory-ram\">Main Memory (RAM)</h4>\n<p>Stores programs and data currently being used.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-1995-h2qcc1-storage\">Storage</h4>\n<p>Stores information permanently.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-1995-h2qcc1-input-and-output-devices\">Input and Output Devices</h4>\n<p>Allow interaction with the outside world.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-1995-h2qcc1-conceptual-diagram\">Conceptual Diagram</h3>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>                 +---------+\n                 |  Input  |\n                 +---------+\n                      |\n                      ↓\n+---------+ &lt;--&gt; +---------+ &lt;--&gt; +----------+\n| Storage |      | Memory  |      |   CPU    |\n+---------+ &lt;--&gt; +---------+ &lt;--&gt; +----------+\n                      |\n                      ↓\n                 +---------+\n                 | Output  |\n                 +---------+</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-1995-h2qcc1-fundamental-idea\">Fundamental Idea</h3>\n<p>Programs and data are stored in memory.  \nThe processor repeatedly:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fetches an instruction.\n</li>\n<li>Executes the instruction.\n</li>\n<li>Moves to the next instruction.\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This idea forms the basis of modern computing.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown"},{"input":"## The Central Processing Unit (CPU)\n\n### What Is the CPU?\n\nCPU stands for:\n\n```text\nCentral Processing Unit\n```\n\nThe CPU is often called:  \nThe brain of the computer.\n\nIts job is to:\n\n- Execute instructions\n- Perform calculations\n- Make decisions\n- Coordinate system activity\n\n### Examples of CPU Tasks\n\nWhen you:\n\n- Open a document\n- Start a video\n- Visit a website\n- Play a game\n\nthe CPU is heavily involved.\n\n### Analogy\n\nImagine a restaurant.  \nThe CPU acts like the head chef.\n\nThe chef:\n\n- Reads orders\n- Coordinates activities\n- Makes decisions\n\nSimilarly, the CPU coordinates computational work.","output":"","result":"The Central Processing Unit (CPU)\nWhat Is the CPU?\nCPU stands for:\nCentral Processing Unit\nThe CPU is often called:  \nThe brain of the computer.\nIts job is to:\n\nExecute instructions\n\nPerform calculations\n\nMake decisions\n\nCoordinate system activity\n\n\nExamples of CPU Tasks\nWhen you:\n\nOpen a document\n\nStart a video\n\nVisit a website\n\nPlay a game\n\n\nthe CPU is heavily involved.\nAnalogy\nImagine a restaurant.  \nThe CPU acts like the head chef.\nThe chef:\n\nReads orders\n\nCoordinates activities\n\nMakes decisions\n\n\nSimilarly, the CPU coordinates computational work.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-1996-qbt8b8-the-central-processing-unit-cpu\">The Central Processing Unit (CPU)</h2>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-1996-qbt8b8-what-is-the-cpu\">What Is the CPU?</h3>\n<p>CPU stands for:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Central Processing Unit</code></pre>\n<p>The CPU is often called:  \nThe brain of the computer.</p>\n<p>Its job is to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Execute instructions\n</li>\n<li>Perform calculations\n</li>\n<li>Make decisions\n</li>\n<li>Coordinate system activity\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-1996-qbt8b8-examples-of-cpu-tasks\">Examples of CPU Tasks</h3>\n<p>When you:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open a document\n</li>\n<li>Start a video\n</li>\n<li>Visit a website\n</li>\n<li>Play a game\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>the CPU is heavily involved.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-1996-qbt8b8-analogy\">Analogy</h3>\n<p>Imagine a restaurant.  \nThe CPU acts like the head chef.</p>\n<p>The chef:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Reads orders\n</li>\n<li>Coordinates activities\n</li>\n<li>Makes decisions\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Similarly, the CPU coordinates computational work.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown"},{"input":"## Components Inside the CPU\n\nAlthough we often think of the CPU as a single component, it contains several internal parts.\n\n### Registers\n\nRegisters are tiny storage locations inside the processor.\n\nThey store:\n\n- Numbers\n- Addresses\n- Intermediate results\n\nRegisters are extremely fast.\n\n#### Example\n\nSuppose the CPU performs:\n\n```text\n5 + 3\n```\n\nThe values may first be placed in registers.  \nThe result is then stored in another register.\n\n### Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU)\n\nThe ALU performs:\n\n- Addition\n- Subtraction\n- Comparisons\n- Logical operations\n\nExamples:\n\n```text\n5 + 3\n7 > 5\nA AND B\n```\n\nThe ALU is built from logic circuits.\n\n### Control Unit\n\nThe Control Unit coordinates processor activity.\n\nIts responsibilities include:\n\n- Reading instructions\n- Determining what must happen\n- Directing data movement\n\nThink of the Control Unit as the conductor of an orchestra.","output":"","result":"Components Inside the CPU\nAlthough we often think of the CPU as a single component, it contains several internal parts.\nRegisters\nRegisters are tiny storage locations inside the processor.\nThey store:\n\nNumbers\n\nAddresses\n\nIntermediate results\n\n\nRegisters are extremely fast.\nExample\nSuppose the CPU performs:\n5 + 3\nThe values may first be placed in registers.  \nThe result is then stored in another register.\nArithmetic Logic Unit (ALU)\nThe ALU performs:\n\nAddition\n\nSubtraction\n\nComparisons\n\nLogical operations\n\n\nExamples:\n5 + 3\n7 > 5\nA AND B\nThe ALU is built from logic circuits.\nControl Unit\nThe Control Unit coordinates processor activity.\nIts responsibilities include:\n\nReading instructions\n\nDetermining what must happen\n\nDirecting data movement\n\n\nThink of the Control Unit as the conductor of an orchestra.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-1997-6j2xi7-components-inside-the-cpu\">Components Inside the CPU</h2>\n<p>Although we often think of the CPU as a single component, it contains several internal parts.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-1997-6j2xi7-registers\">Registers</h3>\n<p>Registers are tiny storage locations inside the processor.</p>\n<p>They store:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Numbers\n</li>\n<li>Addresses\n</li>\n<li>Intermediate results\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Registers are extremely fast.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-1997-6j2xi7-example\">Example</h4>\n<p>Suppose the CPU performs:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>5 + 3</code></pre>\n<p>The values may first be placed in registers.  \nThe result is then stored in another register.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-1997-6j2xi7-arithmetic-logic-unit-alu\">Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU)</h3>\n<p>The ALU performs:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Addition\n</li>\n<li>Subtraction\n</li>\n<li>Comparisons\n</li>\n<li>Logical operations\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>5 + 3\n7 &gt; 5\nA AND B</code></pre>\n<p>The ALU is built from logic circuits.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-1997-6j2xi7-control-unit\">Control Unit</h3>\n<p>The Control Unit coordinates processor activity.</p>\n<p>Its responsibilities include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Reading instructions\n</li>\n<li>Determining what must happen\n</li>\n<li>Directing data movement\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Think of the Control Unit as the conductor of an orchestra.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown"},{"input":"## Machine Instructions\n\nThe CPU executes very simple instructions.\n\nExamples:\n\n```text\nLOAD\nADD\nSTORE\nJUMP\nCOMPARE\n```\n\nA complex application consists of millions or billions of such instructions.\n\n### Example\n\nSuppose we wish to compute:\n\n```text\n2 + 3\n```\n\nThe processor may execute instructions similar to:\n\n```text\nLOAD 2\nLOAD 3\nADD\nSTORE RESULT\n```\n\nEvery task ultimately reduces to basic operations.","output":"","result":"Machine Instructions\nThe CPU executes very simple instructions.\nExamples:\nLOAD\nADD\nSTORE\nJUMP\nCOMPARE\nA complex application consists of millions or billions of such instructions.\nExample\nSuppose we wish to compute:\n2 + 3\nThe processor may execute instructions similar to:\nLOAD 2\nLOAD 3\nADD\nSTORE RESULT\nEvery task ultimately reduces to basic operations.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-1998-1nmofrb-machine-instructions\">Machine Instructions</h2>\n<p>The CPU executes very simple instructions.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>LOAD\nADD\nSTORE\nJUMP\nCOMPARE</code></pre>\n<p>A complex application consists of millions or billions of such instructions.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-1998-1nmofrb-example\">Example</h3>\n<p>Suppose we wish to compute:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>2 + 3</code></pre>\n<p>The processor may execute instructions similar to:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>LOAD 2\nLOAD 3\nADD\nSTORE RESULT</code></pre>\n<p>Every task ultimately reduces to basic operations.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown"},{"input":"## The Fetch-Decode-Execute Cycle\n\nThe CPU continuously repeats the same cycle.\n\n### Step 1: Fetch\n\nRetrieve the next instruction from memory.\n\n```text\nMemory → CPU\n```\n\n### Step 2: Decode\n\nDetermine the meaning of the instruction.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nADD\n```\n\nmeans:\n\n```text\nPerform an addition.\n```\n\n### Step 3: Execute\n\nPerform the requested action.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\n7 + 2 = 9\n```\n\n### Repeat\n\nThe next instruction is then processed.\n\n```text\nFetch\n↓\nDecode\n↓\nExecute\n↓\nRepeat\n```\n\nMillions or billions of times per second.","output":"","result":"The Fetch-Decode-Execute Cycle\nThe CPU continuously repeats the same cycle.\nStep 1: Fetch\nRetrieve the next instruction from memory.\nMemory → CPU\nStep 2: Decode\nDetermine the meaning of the instruction.\nExample:\nADD\nmeans:\nPerform an addition.\nStep 3: Execute\nPerform the requested action.\nExample:\n7 + 2 = 9\nRepeat\nThe next instruction is then processed.\nFetch\n↓\nDecode\n↓\nExecute\n↓\nRepeat\nMillions or billions of times per second.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-1999-38p683-the-fetch-decode-execute-cycle\">The Fetch-Decode-Execute Cycle</h2>\n<p>The CPU continuously repeats the same cycle.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-1999-38p683-step-1-fetch\">Step 1: Fetch</h3>\n<p>Retrieve the next instruction from memory.</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Memory → CPU</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-1999-38p683-step-2-decode\">Step 2: Decode</h3>\n<p>Determine the meaning of the instruction.</p>\n<p>Example:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>ADD</code></pre>\n<p>means:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Perform an addition.</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-1999-38p683-step-3-execute\">Step 3: Execute</h3>\n<p>Perform the requested action.</p>\n<p>Example:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>7 + 2 = 9</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-1999-38p683-repeat\">Repeat</h3>\n<p>The next instruction is then processed.</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Fetch\n↓\nDecode\n↓\nExecute\n↓\nRepeat</code></pre>\n<p>Millions or billions of times per second.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown"},{"input":"## Main Memory (RAM)\n\n### What Is RAM?\n\nRAM stands for:\n\n```text\nRandom Access Memory\n```\n\nRAM stores information currently being used.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Open documents\n- Running programs\n- Web pages\n\n### Characteristics\n\n#### Fast\n\nThe CPU can access RAM quickly.\n\n#### Temporary\n\nRAM loses its contents when power is removed.\n\n### Analogy\n\nThink of RAM as a work desk.  \nInformation currently needed is placed on the desk.  \nWhen work is finished, the desk is cleared.","output":"","result":"Main Memory (RAM)\nWhat Is RAM?\nRAM stands for:\nRandom Access Memory\nRAM stores information currently being used.\nExamples:\n\nOpen documents\n\nRunning programs\n\nWeb pages\n\n\nCharacteristics\nFast\nThe CPU can access RAM quickly.\nTemporary\nRAM loses its contents when power is removed.\nAnalogy\nThink of RAM as a work desk.  \nInformation currently needed is placed on the desk.  \nWhen work is finished, the desk is cleared.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-2000-sxfhiy-main-memory-ram\">Main Memory (RAM)</h2>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2000-sxfhiy-what-is-ram\">What Is RAM?</h3>\n<p>RAM stands for:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Random Access Memory</code></pre>\n<p>RAM stores information currently being used.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open documents\n</li>\n<li>Running programs\n</li>\n<li>Web pages\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2000-sxfhiy-characteristics\">Characteristics</h3>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-2000-sxfhiy-fast\">Fast</h4>\n<p>The CPU can access RAM quickly.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-2000-sxfhiy-temporary\">Temporary</h4>\n<p>RAM loses its contents when power is removed.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2000-sxfhiy-analogy\">Analogy</h3>\n<p>Think of RAM as a work desk.  \nInformation currently needed is placed on the desk.  \nWhen work is finished, the desk is cleared.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown"},{"input":"## Secondary Storage\n\nStorage retains information permanently.\n\nExamples:\n\n- SSDs\n- Hard Disks\n- USB Drives\n\n### Characteristics\n\n#### Large Capacity\n\nCan store enormous amounts of information.\n\n#### Permanent\n\nData remains available when power is removed.\n\n#### Slower Than RAM\n\nStorage is much slower than main memory.\n\n### Analogy\n\nStorage is like a filing cabinet.  \nInformation can be stored there indefinitely.  \nHowever, retrieving information takes longer than retrieving it from a desk.","output":"","result":"Secondary Storage\nStorage retains information permanently.\nExamples:\n\nSSDs\n\nHard Disks\n\nUSB Drives\n\n\nCharacteristics\nLarge Capacity\nCan store enormous amounts of information.\nPermanent\nData remains available when power is removed.\nSlower Than RAM\nStorage is much slower than main memory.\nAnalogy\nStorage is like a filing cabinet.  \nInformation can be stored there indefinitely.  \nHowever, retrieving information takes longer than retrieving it from a desk.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-2001-z73p7t-secondary-storage\">Secondary Storage</h2>\n<p>Storage retains information permanently.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>SSDs\n</li>\n<li>Hard Disks\n</li>\n<li>USB Drives\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2001-z73p7t-characteristics\">Characteristics</h3>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-2001-z73p7t-large-capacity\">Large Capacity</h4>\n<p>Can store enormous amounts of information.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-2001-z73p7t-permanent\">Permanent</h4>\n<p>Data remains available when power is removed.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-2001-z73p7t-slower-than-ram\">Slower Than RAM</h4>\n<p>Storage is much slower than main memory.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2001-z73p7t-analogy\">Analogy</h3>\n<p>Storage is like a filing cabinet.  \nInformation can be stored there indefinitely.  \nHowever, retrieving information takes longer than retrieving it from a desk.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown"},{"input":"## Why Programs Must Be Loaded Into RAM\n\nA common misconception is that processors execute programs directly from storage.  \nThey do not.\n\n### Program Startup\n\n#### Step 1\n\nLocate program on storage.\n\n```text\nSSD\n```\n\n#### Step 2\n\nCopy program into RAM.\n\n```text\nSSD → RAM\n```\n\n#### Step 3\n\nCPU executes instructions from RAM.\n\n```text\nRAM → CPU\n```\n\n### Why?\n\nRAM is much faster than storage.  \nWithout RAM, computers would feel extremely slow.","output":"","result":"Why Programs Must Be Loaded Into RAM\nA common misconception is that processors execute programs directly from storage.  \nThey do not.\nProgram Startup\nStep 1\nLocate program on storage.\nSSD\nStep 2\nCopy program into RAM.\nSSD → RAM\nStep 3\nCPU executes instructions from RAM.\nRAM → CPU\nWhy?\nRAM is much faster than storage.  \nWithout RAM, computers would feel extremely slow.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-2002-docfri-why-programs-must-be-loaded-into-ram\">Why Programs Must Be Loaded Into RAM</h2>\n<p>A common misconception is that processors execute programs directly from storage.  \nThey do not.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2002-docfri-program-startup\">Program Startup</h3>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-2002-docfri-step-1\">Step 1</h4>\n<p>Locate program on storage.</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>SSD</code></pre>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-2002-docfri-step-2\">Step 2</h4>\n<p>Copy program into RAM.</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>SSD → RAM</code></pre>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-2002-docfri-step-3\">Step 3</h4>\n<p>CPU executes instructions from RAM.</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>RAM → CPU</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2002-docfri-why\">Why?</h3>\n<p>RAM is much faster than storage.  \nWithout RAM, computers would feel extremely slow.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown"},{"input":"## The Memory Hierarchy\n\nNot all memory is equally fast.  \nComputers use multiple layers of memory.\n\n### Hierarchy\n\n```text\nRegisters\n↓\nCache\n↓\nRAM\n↓\nStorage\n```\n\n### Characteristics\n\nAs we move downward:\n\n```text\nCapacity increases\nSpeed decreases\nCost decreases\n```\n\n### Visualization\n\n```text\nFast / Small\n\nRegisters\n\nCache\n\nRAM\n\nStorage\n\nSlow / Large\n```\n\n\n","output":"","result":"The Memory Hierarchy\nNot all memory is equally fast.  \nComputers use multiple layers of memory.\nHierarchy\nRegisters\n↓\nCache\n↓\nRAM\n↓\nStorage\nCharacteristics\nAs we move downward:\nCapacity increases\nSpeed decreases\nCost decreases\nVisualization\nFast / Small\n\nRegisters\n\nCache\n\nRAM\n\nStorage\n\nSlow / Large","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-2003-1w8pt8o-the-memory-hierarchy\">The Memory Hierarchy</h2>\n<p>Not all memory is equally fast.  \nComputers use multiple layers of memory.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2003-1w8pt8o-hierarchy\">Hierarchy</h3>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Registers\n↓\nCache\n↓\nRAM\n↓\nStorage</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2003-1w8pt8o-characteristics\">Characteristics</h3>\n<p>As we move downward:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Capacity increases\nSpeed decreases\nCost decreases</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2003-1w8pt8o-visualization\">Visualization</h3>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Fast / Small\n\nRegisters\n\nCache\n\nRAM\n\nStorage\n\nSlow / Large</code></pre>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown"},{"input":"## Cache Memory\n\nCache is a small but extremely fast memory located close to the CPU.\n\n### Purpose\n\nFrequently used information is kept in cache.  \nThis reduces waiting time.\n\n### Analogy\n\nImagine studying.\n\n#### Desk\n\nFrequently used books.\n\n#### Bookshelf\n\nLess frequently used books.\n\n#### Library\n\nEverything else.\n\nCache behaves like the desk.  \nRAM behaves like the bookshelf.  \nStorage behaves like the library.\n\n### Why Cache Matters\n\nModern processors are much faster than RAM.\n\nWithout cache:\n\n```text\nCPU waits frequently\n```\n\nCache reduces these delays.","output":"","result":"Cache Memory\nCache is a small but extremely fast memory located close to the CPU.\nPurpose\nFrequently used information is kept in cache.  \nThis reduces waiting time.\nAnalogy\nImagine studying.\nDesk\nFrequently used books.\nBookshelf\nLess frequently used books.\nLibrary\nEverything else.\nCache behaves like the desk.  \nRAM behaves like the bookshelf.  \nStorage behaves like the library.\nWhy Cache Matters\nModern processors are much faster than RAM.\nWithout cache:\nCPU waits frequently\nCache reduces these delays.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-2004-d36ea4-cache-memory\">Cache Memory</h2>\n<p>Cache is a small but extremely fast memory located close to the CPU.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2004-d36ea4-purpose\">Purpose</h3>\n<p>Frequently used information is kept in cache.  \nThis reduces waiting time.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2004-d36ea4-analogy\">Analogy</h3>\n<p>Imagine studying.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-2004-d36ea4-desk\">Desk</h4>\n<p>Frequently used books.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-2004-d36ea4-bookshelf\">Bookshelf</h4>\n<p>Less frequently used books.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-2004-d36ea4-library\">Library</h4>\n<p>Everything else.</p>\n<p>Cache behaves like the desk.  \nRAM behaves like the bookshelf.  \nStorage behaves like the library.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2004-d36ea4-why-cache-matters\">Why Cache Matters</h3>\n<p>Modern processors are much faster than RAM.</p>\n<p>Without cache:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>CPU waits frequently</code></pre>\n<p>Cache reduces these delays.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown"},{"input":"## Input and Output Devices\n\nComputers interact with the outside world through input and output devices.\n\n### Input Devices\n\nExamples:\n\n- Keyboard\n- Mouse\n- Touchscreen\n- Microphone\n- Camera\n\nInput devices provide data to the computer.\n\n### Output Devices\n\nExamples:\n\n- Monitor\n- Printer\n- Speakers\n- Headphones\n\nOutput devices present results.\n\n### Example\n\nWriting a document:\n\n```text\nKeyboard → Input\n\nCPU → Processing\n\nMonitor → Output\n\nStorage → Save File\n```","output":"","result":"Input and Output Devices\nComputers interact with the outside world through input and output devices.\nInput Devices\nExamples:\n\nKeyboard\n\nMouse\n\nTouchscreen\n\nMicrophone\n\nCamera\n\n\nInput devices provide data to the computer.\nOutput Devices\nExamples:\n\nMonitor\n\nPrinter\n\nSpeakers\n\nHeadphones\n\n\nOutput devices present results.\nExample\nWriting a document:\nKeyboard → Input\n\nCPU → Processing\n\nMonitor → Output\n\nStorage → Save File","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-2005-xfkha1-input-and-output-devices\">Input and Output Devices</h2>\n<p>Computers interact with the outside world through input and output devices.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2005-xfkha1-input-devices\">Input Devices</h3>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Keyboard\n</li>\n<li>Mouse\n</li>\n<li>Touchscreen\n</li>\n<li>Microphone\n</li>\n<li>Camera\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Input devices provide data to the computer.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2005-xfkha1-output-devices\">Output Devices</h3>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Monitor\n</li>\n<li>Printer\n</li>\n<li>Speakers\n</li>\n<li>Headphones\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Output devices present results.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2005-xfkha1-example\">Example</h3>\n<p>Writing a document:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Keyboard → Input\n\nCPU → Processing\n\nMonitor → Output\n\nStorage → Save File</code></pre>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown"},{"input":"## Communication Inside the Computer\n\nComputer components must exchange information.\n\n### Buses\n\nA bus is a communication pathway connecting components.  \nThink of a bus as a highway.\n\n### Example\n\n```text\nCPU ↔ RAM\n\nCPU ↔ Storage\n\nCPU ↔ Graphics Card\n```\n\nData travels along these connections.\n\n### Why Communication Matters\n\nEven fast processors become ineffective if data cannot reach them quickly.  \nPerformance depends on communication as well as computation.","output":"","result":"Communication Inside the Computer\nComputer components must exchange information.\nBuses\nA bus is a communication pathway connecting components.  \nThink of a bus as a highway.\nExample\nCPU ↔ RAM\n\nCPU ↔ Storage\n\nCPU ↔ Graphics Card\nData travels along these connections.\nWhy Communication Matters\nEven fast processors become ineffective if data cannot reach them quickly.  \nPerformance depends on communication as well as computation.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-2006-yedq0z-communication-inside-the-computer\">Communication Inside the Computer</h2>\n<p>Computer components must exchange information.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2006-yedq0z-buses\">Buses</h3>\n<p>A bus is a communication pathway connecting components.  \nThink of a bus as a highway.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2006-yedq0z-example\">Example</h3>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>CPU ↔ RAM\n\nCPU ↔ Storage\n\nCPU ↔ Graphics Card</code></pre>\n<p>Data travels along these connections.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2006-yedq0z-why-communication-matters\">Why Communication Matters</h3>\n<p>Even fast processors become ineffective if data cannot reach them quickly.  \nPerformance depends on communication as well as computation.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown"},{"input":"## Graphics Processing Units (GPUs)\n\nModern computers often include a GPU.\n\nGPU stands for:\n\n```text\nGraphics Processing Unit\n```\n\n### Original Purpose\n\nGPUs were designed for:\n\n- Graphics\n- Video rendering\n- Games\n\n### Modern Uses\n\nToday GPUs are heavily used for:\n\n- Scientific computation\n- Machine learning\n- Artificial intelligence\n\n### CPU versus GPU\n\n#### CPU\n\nExcellent at:\n\n- General-purpose tasks\n- Decision making\n- Complex instruction flow\n\n#### GPU\n\nExcellent at:\n\n- Repeating the same calculation many times\n- Parallel processing\n\n### Example\n\nRendering millions of pixels simultaneously is ideal for a GPU.","output":"","result":"Graphics Processing Units (GPUs)\nModern computers often include a GPU.\nGPU stands for:\nGraphics Processing Unit\nOriginal Purpose\nGPUs were designed for:\n\nGraphics\n\nVideo rendering\n\nGames\n\n\nModern Uses\nToday GPUs are heavily used for:\n\nScientific computation\n\nMachine learning\n\nArtificial intelligence\n\n\nCPU versus GPU\nCPU\nExcellent at:\n\nGeneral-purpose tasks\n\nDecision making\n\nComplex instruction flow\n\n\nGPU\nExcellent at:\n\nRepeating the same calculation many times\n\nParallel processing\n\n\nExample\nRendering millions of pixels simultaneously is ideal for a GPU.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-2007-8ev6el-graphics-processing-units-gpus\">Graphics Processing Units (GPUs)</h2>\n<p>Modern computers often include a GPU.</p>\n<p>GPU stands for:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Graphics Processing Unit</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2007-8ev6el-original-purpose\">Original Purpose</h3>\n<p>GPUs were designed for:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Graphics\n</li>\n<li>Video rendering\n</li>\n<li>Games\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2007-8ev6el-modern-uses\">Modern Uses</h3>\n<p>Today GPUs are heavily used for:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Scientific computation\n</li>\n<li>Machine learning\n</li>\n<li>Artificial intelligence\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2007-8ev6el-cpu-versus-gpu\">CPU versus GPU</h3>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-2007-8ev6el-cpu\">CPU</h4>\n<p>Excellent at:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>General-purpose tasks\n</li>\n<li>Decision making\n</li>\n<li>Complex instruction flow\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-2007-8ev6el-gpu\">GPU</h4>\n<p>Excellent at:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Repeating the same calculation many times\n</li>\n<li>Parallel processing\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2007-8ev6el-example\">Example</h3>\n<p>Rendering millions of pixels simultaneously is ideal for a GPU.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown"},{"input":"## Specialized Processors\n\nModern systems contain many processors.\n\nExamples include:\n\n#### Network Controllers\n\nManage communications.\n\n#### Audio Processors\n\nHandle sound processing.\n\n#### AI Accelerators\n\nOptimize machine learning workloads.\n\n#### Embedded Controllers\n\nManage keyboards, batteries, sensors, and displays.\n\n### Key Observation\n\nA modern computer is not one processor.  \nIt is often a collection of specialized processors cooperating together.","output":"","result":"Specialized Processors\nModern systems contain many processors.\nExamples include:\nNetwork Controllers\nManage communications.\nAudio Processors\nHandle sound processing.\nAI Accelerators\nOptimize machine learning workloads.\nEmbedded Controllers\nManage keyboards, batteries, sensors, and displays.\nKey Observation\nA modern computer is not one processor.  \nIt is often a collection of specialized processors cooperating together.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-2008-dq4he7-specialized-processors\">Specialized Processors</h2>\n<p>Modern systems contain many processors.</p>\n<p>Examples include:</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-2008-dq4he7-network-controllers\">Network Controllers</h4>\n<p>Manage communications.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-2008-dq4he7-audio-processors\">Audio Processors</h4>\n<p>Handle sound processing.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-2008-dq4he7-ai-accelerators\">AI Accelerators</h4>\n<p>Optimize machine learning workloads.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-2008-dq4he7-embedded-controllers\">Embedded Controllers</h4>\n<p>Manage keyboards, batteries, sensors, and displays.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2008-dq4he7-key-observation\">Key Observation</h3>\n<p>A modern computer is not one processor.  \nIt is often a collection of specialized processors cooperating together.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown"},{"input":"## Putting Everything Together\n\nSuppose you open a web browser.\n\n### Step 1\n\nBrowser stored on SSD.\n\n```text\nStorage\n```\n\n### Step 2\n\nProgram loaded into RAM.\n\n```text\nRAM\n```\n\n### Step 3\n\nCPU begins executing instructions.\n\n```text\nCPU\n```\n\n### Step 4\n\nData arrives from the Internet.\n\n```text\nNetwork Interface\n```\n\n### Step 5\n\nImages displayed on screen.\n\n```text\nGPU + Monitor\n```\n\n### Step 6\n\nSound played through speakers.\n\n```text\nAudio Hardware\n```\n\nMany hardware components cooperate to perform what appears to be a simple task.","output":"","result":"Putting Everything Together\nSuppose you open a web browser.\nStep 1\nBrowser stored on SSD.\nStorage\nStep 2\nProgram loaded into RAM.\nRAM\nStep 3\nCPU begins executing instructions.\nCPU\nStep 4\nData arrives from the Internet.\nNetwork Interface\nStep 5\nImages displayed on screen.\nGPU + Monitor\nStep 6\nSound played through speakers.\nAudio Hardware\nMany hardware components cooperate to perform what appears to be a simple task.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-2009-1evy8o-putting-everything-together\">Putting Everything Together</h2>\n<p>Suppose you open a web browser.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2009-1evy8o-step-1\">Step 1</h3>\n<p>Browser stored on SSD.</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Storage</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2009-1evy8o-step-2\">Step 2</h3>\n<p>Program loaded into RAM.</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>RAM</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2009-1evy8o-step-3\">Step 3</h3>\n<p>CPU begins executing instructions.</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>CPU</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2009-1evy8o-step-4\">Step 4</h3>\n<p>Data arrives from the Internet.</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Network Interface</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2009-1evy8o-step-5\">Step 5</h3>\n<p>Images displayed on screen.</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>GPU + Monitor</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-2009-1evy8o-step-6\">Step 6</h3>\n<p>Sound played through speakers.</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Audio Hardware</code></pre>\n<p>Many hardware components cooperate to perform what appears to be a simple task.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown"},{"input":"## Summary\n\nIn this chapter we learned:\n\n- Most computers follow the Von Neumann architecture.\n- The CPU executes instructions.\n- Registers provide the fastest storage inside the processor.\n- The ALU performs arithmetic and logical operations.\n- The Control Unit coordinates execution.\n- Programs are executed using the fetch-decode-execute cycle.\n- RAM stores currently active programs and data.\n- Storage retains information permanently.\n- Memory is organized as a hierarchy.\n- Cache improves performance.\n- Input and output devices connect computers with their environment.\n- Buses allow components to communicate.\n- GPUs and specialized processors perform specific tasks efficiently.","output":"","result":"Summary\nIn this chapter we learned:\n\nMost computers follow the Von Neumann architecture.\n\nThe CPU executes instructions.\n\nRegisters provide the fastest storage inside the processor.\n\nThe ALU performs arithmetic and logical operations.\n\nThe Control Unit coordinates execution.\n\nPrograms are executed using the fetch-decode-execute cycle.\n\nRAM stores currently active programs and data.\n\nStorage retains information permanently.\n\nMemory is organized as a hierarchy.\n\nCache improves performance.\n\nInput and output devices connect computers with their environment.\n\nBuses allow components to communicate.\n\nGPUs and specialized processors perform specific tasks efficiently.\n\n","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-2010-368n9i-summary\">Summary</h2>\n<p>In this chapter we learned:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Most computers follow the Von Neumann architecture.\n</li>\n<li>The CPU executes instructions.\n</li>\n<li>Registers provide the fastest storage inside the processor.\n</li>\n<li>The ALU performs arithmetic and logical operations.\n</li>\n<li>The Control Unit coordinates execution.\n</li>\n<li>Programs are executed using the fetch-decode-execute cycle.\n</li>\n<li>RAM stores currently active programs and data.\n</li>\n<li>Storage retains information permanently.\n</li>\n<li>Memory is organized as a hierarchy.\n</li>\n<li>Cache improves performance.\n</li>\n<li>Input and output devices connect computers with their environment.\n</li>\n<li>Buses allow components to communicate.\n</li>\n<li>GPUs and specialized processors perform specific tasks efficiently.\n</li>\n</ul>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown"},{"input":"## Key Terms\n\n| Term                       | Definition                                                   |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Von Neumann Architecture   | Classical computer architecture with processor, memory, and storage |\n| CPU                        | Central Processing Unit                                      |\n| Register                   | Small high-speed storage location inside the CPU             |\n| ALU                        | Arithmetic Logic Unit                                        |\n| Control Unit               | CPU component that coordinates execution                     |\n| Machine Instruction        | Basic command executed by the CPU                            |\n| Fetch-Decode-Execute Cycle | Repeating process used to execute instructions               |\n| RAM                        | Random Access Memory                                         |\n| Cache                      | Small, fast memory located near the CPU                      |\n| Storage                    | Permanent data retention                                     |\n| Bus                        | Communication pathway between components                     |\n| GPU                        | Graphics Processing Unit                                     |\n| Memory Hierarchy           | Organization of memory by speed and capacity                 |","output":"","result":"Key Terms\nTermDefinitionVon Neumann ArchitectureClassical computer architecture with processor, memory, and storageCPUCentral Processing UnitRegisterSmall high-speed storage location inside the CPUALUArithmetic Logic UnitControl UnitCPU component that coordinates executionMachine InstructionBasic command executed by the CPUFetch-Decode-Execute CycleRepeating process used to execute instructionsRAMRandom Access MemoryCacheSmall, fast memory located near the CPUStoragePermanent data retentionBusCommunication pathway between componentsGPUGraphics Processing UnitMemory HierarchyOrganization of memory by speed and capacity","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-2011-5em0gy-key-terms\">Key Terms</h2>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Term</th><th>Definition</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Von Neumann Architecture</td><td>Classical computer architecture with processor, memory, and storage</td></tr><tr><td>CPU</td><td>Central Processing Unit</td></tr><tr><td>Register</td><td>Small high-speed storage location inside the CPU</td></tr><tr><td>ALU</td><td>Arithmetic Logic Unit</td></tr><tr><td>Control Unit</td><td>CPU component that coordinates execution</td></tr><tr><td>Machine Instruction</td><td>Basic command executed by the CPU</td></tr><tr><td>Fetch-Decode-Execute Cycle</td><td>Repeating process used to execute instructions</td></tr><tr><td>RAM</td><td>Random Access Memory</td></tr><tr><td>Cache</td><td>Small, fast memory located near the CPU</td></tr><tr><td>Storage</td><td>Permanent data retention</td></tr><tr><td>Bus</td><td>Communication pathway between components</td></tr><tr><td>GPU</td><td>Graphics Processing Unit</td></tr><tr><td>Memory Hierarchy</td><td>Organization of memory by speed and capacity</td></tr></tbody></table>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown"},{"input":"## Review Questions\n\n- What are the main components of the Von Neumann architecture?\n- What is the role of the CPU?\n- What is the difference between a register and RAM?\n- What does the ALU do?\n- What is the purpose of the Control Unit?\n- Describe the fetch-decode-execute cycle.\n- Why must programs be loaded into RAM before execution?\n- What is the purpose of cache memory?\n- How does storage differ from RAM?\n- What is a bus?\n- Why are GPUs useful?\n- Explain the memory hierarchy from registers to storage.\n- What happens inside a computer when an application is opened?","output":"","result":"Review Questions\n\nWhat are the main components of the Von Neumann architecture?\n\nWhat is the role of the CPU?\n\nWhat is the difference between a register and RAM?\n\nWhat does the ALU do?\n\nWhat is the purpose of the Control Unit?\n\nDescribe the fetch-decode-execute cycle.\n\nWhy must programs be loaded into RAM before execution?\n\nWhat is the purpose of cache memory?\n\nHow does storage differ from RAM?\n\nWhat is a bus?\n\nWhy are GPUs useful?\n\nExplain the memory hierarchy from registers to storage.\n\nWhat happens inside a computer when an application is opened?\n\n","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-2012-119a1w5-review-questions\">Review Questions</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>What are the main components of the Von Neumann architecture?\n</li>\n<li>What is the role of the CPU?\n</li>\n<li>What is the difference between a register and RAM?\n</li>\n<li>What does the ALU do?\n</li>\n<li>What is the purpose of the Control Unit?\n</li>\n<li>Describe the fetch-decode-execute cycle.\n</li>\n<li>Why must programs be loaded into RAM before execution?\n</li>\n<li>What is the purpose of cache memory?\n</li>\n<li>How does storage differ from RAM?\n</li>\n<li>What is a bus?\n</li>\n<li>Why are GPUs useful?\n</li>\n<li>Explain the memory hierarchy from registers to storage.\n</li>\n<li>What happens inside a computer when an application is opened?\n</li>\n</ul>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown"},{"input":"## Transition to Lecture 5\n\nWe now understand how computer hardware executes instructions. But where do those instructions come from?  \nIn the next chapter, we will explore **software, machine code, assembly language, and the connection between human-written programs and the hardware that executes them.**","output":"","result":"Transition to Lecture 5\nWe now understand how computer hardware executes instructions. But where do those instructions come from?  \nIn the next chapter, we will explore software, machine code, assembly language, and the connection between human-written programs and the hardware that executes them.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-2013-4rakn2-transition-to-lecture-5\">Transition to Lecture 5</h2>\n<p>We now understand how computer hardware executes instructions. But where do those instructions come from?  \nIn the next chapter, we will explore <strong>software, machine code, assembly language, and the connection between human-written programs and the hardware that executes them.</strong></p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown"},{"input":"## Lexicon\n\n| English                  | Dutch                        | French                             |\n| ------------------------ | ---------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| Computer Architecture    | de computerarchitectuur      | l'architecture informatique (f.)   |\n| Von Neumann Architecture | de Von Neumann-architectuur  | l'architecture de Von Neumann (f.) |\n| CPU                      | de CPU                       | le CPU (m.)                        |\n| Processor                | de processor                 | le processeur (m.)                 |\n| Control Unit             | de besturingseenheid         | l'unité de contrôle (f.)           |\n| Machine Instruction      | de machine-instructie        | l'instruction machine (f.)         |\n| Fetch                    | het ophalen                  | l'extraction (f.)                  |\n| Decode                   | het decoderen                | le décodage (m.)                   |\n| Execute                  | het uitvoeren                | l'exécution (f.)                   |\n| RAM                      | het werkgeheugen             | la mémoire vive (f.)               |\n| Main Memory              | het hoofdgeheugen            | la mémoire principale (f.)         |\n| Secondary Storage        | de secundaire opslag         | le stockage secondaire (m.)        |\n| SSD                      | de SSD                       | le SSD (m.)                        |\n| Hard Disk Drive          | de harde schijf              | le disque dur (m.)                 |\n| Memory Hierarchy         | de geheugenhiërarchie        | la hiérarchie mémoire (f.)         |\n| Cache Memory             | het cachegeheugen            | la mémoire cache (f.)              |\n| Input Device             | het invoerapparaat           | le périphérique d'entrée (m.)      |\n| Output Device            | het uitvoerapparaat          | le périphérique de sortie (m.)     |\n| Bus                      | de bus                       | le bus (m.)                        |\n| Data Bus                 | de databus                   | le bus de données (m.)             |\n| GPU                      | de GPU                       | le processeur graphique (m.)       |\n| Accelerator              | de versneller                | l'accélérateur (m.)                |\n| Performance              | de prestatie                 | la performance (f.)                |\n| Bottleneck               | de bottleneck / het knelpunt | le goulot d'étranglement (m.)      |","output":"","result":"Lexicon\nEnglishDutchFrenchComputer Architecturede computerarchitectuurl’architecture informatique (f.)Von Neumann Architecturede Von Neumann-architectuurl’architecture de Von Neumann (f.)CPUde CPUle CPU (m.)Processorde processorle processeur (m.)Control Unitde besturingseenheidl’unité de contrôle (f.)Machine Instructionde machine-instructiel’instruction machine (f.)Fetchhet ophalenl’extraction (f.)Decodehet decoderenle décodage (m.)Executehet uitvoerenl’exécution (f.)RAMhet werkgeheugenla mémoire vive (f.)Main Memoryhet hoofdgeheugenla mémoire principale (f.)Secondary Storagede secundaire opslagle stockage secondaire (m.)SSDde SSDle SSD (m.)Hard Disk Drivede harde schijfle disque dur (m.)Memory Hierarchyde geheugenhiërarchiela hiérarchie mémoire (f.)Cache Memoryhet cachegeheugenla mémoire cache (f.)Input Devicehet invoerapparaatle périphérique d’entrée (m.)Output Devicehet uitvoerapparaatle périphérique de sortie (m.)Busde busle bus (m.)Data Busde databusle bus de données (m.)GPUde GPUle processeur graphique (m.)Acceleratorde versnellerl’accélérateur (m.)Performancede prestatiela performance (f.)Bottleneckde bottleneck / het knelpuntle goulot d’étranglement (m.)","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-2014-1pfymsy-lexicon\">Lexicon</h2>\n<table><thead><tr><th>English</th><th>Dutch</th><th>French</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Computer Architecture</td><td>de computerarchitectuur</td><td>l’architecture informatique (f.)</td></tr><tr><td>Von Neumann Architecture</td><td>de Von Neumann-architectuur</td><td>l’architecture de Von Neumann (f.)</td></tr><tr><td>CPU</td><td>de CPU</td><td>le CPU (m.)</td></tr><tr><td>Processor</td><td>de processor</td><td>le processeur (m.)</td></tr><tr><td>Control Unit</td><td>de besturingseenheid</td><td>l’unité de contrôle (f.)</td></tr><tr><td>Machine Instruction</td><td>de machine-instructie</td><td>l’instruction machine (f.)</td></tr><tr><td>Fetch</td><td>het ophalen</td><td>l’extraction (f.)</td></tr><tr><td>Decode</td><td>het decoderen</td><td>le décodage (m.)</td></tr><tr><td>Execute</td><td>het uitvoeren</td><td>l’exécution (f.)</td></tr><tr><td>RAM</td><td>het werkgeheugen</td><td>la mémoire vive (f.)</td></tr><tr><td>Main Memory</td><td>het hoofdgeheugen</td><td>la mémoire principale (f.)</td></tr><tr><td>Secondary Storage</td><td>de secundaire opslag</td><td>le stockage secondaire (m.)</td></tr><tr><td>SSD</td><td>de SSD</td><td>le SSD (m.)</td></tr><tr><td>Hard Disk Drive</td><td>de harde schijf</td><td>le disque dur (m.)</td></tr><tr><td>Memory Hierarchy</td><td>de geheugenhiërarchie</td><td>la hiérarchie mémoire (f.)</td></tr><tr><td>Cache Memory</td><td>het cachegeheugen</td><td>la mémoire cache (f.)</td></tr><tr><td>Input Device</td><td>het invoerapparaat</td><td>le périphérique d’entrée (m.)</td></tr><tr><td>Output Device</td><td>het uitvoerapparaat</td><td>le périphérique de sortie (m.)</td></tr><tr><td>Bus</td><td>de bus</td><td>le bus (m.)</td></tr><tr><td>Data Bus</td><td>de databus</td><td>le bus de données (m.)</td></tr><tr><td>GPU</td><td>de GPU</td><td>le processeur graphique (m.)</td></tr><tr><td>Accelerator</td><td>de versneller</td><td>l’accélérateur (m.)</td></tr><tr><td>Performance</td><td>de prestatie</td><td>la performance (f.)</td></tr><tr><td>Bottleneck</td><td>de bottleneck / het knelpunt</td><td>le goulot d’étranglement (m.)</td></tr></tbody></table>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown"}]